  "facts": [
    "The Peace Bridge, completed in 1927, spans 5,800 feet over the Niagara River, featuring five arched steel spans and a Parker deck truss, a marvel of early 20th-century engineering.",
    "On March 13, 1927, chief engineer Edward Lupfer drove the first car across the bridge, marking a historic moment that celebrated a century of peace between the United States and Canada.",
    "In 2005, the Canadian side installed E‑ZPass, making the Peace Bridge the first North American bridge outside the U.S. to accept the electronic toll system, while U.S. entry remains toll-free."
